{0 Services}

Services are the entry points of a Web site. A service is usually attached to
a URL, and it generates a page.

- {{!//server/services/page-types}The different types of services}: services
  with a path, pathless and attached services, and how Eliom finds the service
  a request is for.
- {{!//server/services/page-parameters}Typing service parameters}: GET and
  POST parameters, decoded and checked against their types.
- {{!//server/services/page-handlers}Service handlers}: the output modules,
  which decide what a handler returns (HTML pages, redirections, actions,
  files, OCaml values), and error handling.
- {{!//server/services/page-links}Creating links and forms}: links and forms
  checked against the parameters of the service they lead to.
